subproblems.statement:
Let m, k ∈ ℕ, n := m + k and P := WithLp 2 (ℝᵐ × ℝᵏ). Let G : ℝⁿ → ℝᵐ be of class C¹, D ⊆ ℝⁿ open, and u₀ ∈ D with DG(u₀) surjective. Then there is an open partial homeomorphism Φ from ℝⁿ to P (Mathlib OpenPartialHomeomorph: a homeomorphism from its open source onto its open target, with inverse Φ.symm) such that:
- u₀ ∈ source(Φ) ⊆ D;
- Φ is C¹ on source(Φ);
- Φ.symm is C¹ on target(Φ);
- the first component of Φ(u) is G(u) for every u ∈ source(Φ).
Notation as in the parent: ℝ^d = Rn d = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d); DG(u₀) = fderiv ℝ G u₀; 'of class C¹' means ContDiff ℝ 1 (on all of ℝⁿ) or ContDiffOn ℝ 1 (on the indicated set).
